From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ps5sd <ps5sd@localhost>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 12:30:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] server: the jobs and their progress as server-sent events

A client saw a job's progress only by polling GET /sdcpp/v1/jobs/<id> or
GET /ps5sd/v1/jobs, and the step count not at all: it went to the
application's activity hooks (the TV) only.

GET /ps5sd/v1/events is a text/event-stream (events.cpp): a "jobs" event with
the queued and generating jobs when the stream opens and whenever they
change, a "progress" event per step (at most four a second: step, steps,
seconds per step, the time left of that phase, the job), a "job" event when
a job ends, and a ": ping" comment every 15 s, so a proxy (Cloudflare gives
up after 100 s) keeps it open. A stream that opens while nothing runs gets no
progress of the run before. ?job=<id> follows one job and ends after its
"job" event. sd_progress_cb, the job worker and the job routes wake the
streams; a change shows at most a second late in any case.

Each stream holds one of cpp-httplib's threads, so at most four are open at
once (429 too_many_streams); a stream whose client went away frees its
thread within a second. sd_server_terminate() ends them, so a model
switch does not wait for a client: measured with the library build, sd_server
returned 1 ms after terminate with a stream open.

